From: Galaxy C5 Forge <forge@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: finish Q6 cleanup outside a fatally signalled task

Baseline: 71b335bed497bbe8b9754c9c986801a66212ce4f

Android 10 shutdown kills the PeripheralManager while it holds the last
modem subsystem fd. Its exit path synchronously invokes the IPA notifier.
CMA allocation can then fail because contiguous migration checks the
caller's pending fatal signal. On c5lte the four-byte DMA allocation fails
and the mandatory cleanup BUGs, causing a panic-driven restart.

Queue the original complete cleanup on system_unbound_wq and flush the
individual work item before returning to subsystem shutdown. Always use
the worker so that a fatal signal arriving after notifier entry cannot
race the dispatch. Use an on-stack work item with matching lifetime
annotations; no cleanup request allocation is needed in the exiting task.
The uninterruptible flush keeps all clocks, commands and DMA-buffer
lifetimes inside the existing notifier ordering. Preserve every original
cleanup step and fatal error check. No caller-owned mutex is released by
the cleanup; its locks are acquired and released within the worker.

The log confirms allocation failure and panic; it does not print CMA's
numeric errno. The signal-interruption mechanism is source-supported and
must still be confirmed by the shutdown hardware regression.

diff --git a/drivers/platform/msm/ipa/ipa.c b/drivers/platform/msm/ipa/ipa.c
index ac8fa733..77ca7534 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/msm/ipa/ipa.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/msm/ipa/ipa.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/rbtree.h>
 #include <linux/uaccess.h>
+#include <linux/workqueue.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/msm-bus.h>
 #include <linux/msm-bus-board.h>
@@ -1868,7 +1869,7 @@ static int ipa_q6_set_ex_path_dis_agg(void)
 }
 
 /**
-* ipa_q6_pre_shutdown_cleanup() - A cleanup for all Q6 related configuration
+* ipa_q6_pre_shutdown_cleanup_impl() - Clean all Q6 related configuration
 *                    in IPA HW before modem shutdown. This is performed in
 *                    case of SSR.
 *
@@ -1877,7 +1878,7 @@ static int ipa_q6_set_ex_path_dis_agg(void)
 * This is a mandatory procedure, in case one of the steps fails, the
 * AP needs to restart.
 */
-int ipa_q6_pre_shutdown_cleanup(void)
+static int ipa_q6_pre_shutdown_cleanup_impl(void)
 {
 	/* If uC has notified the APPS upon a ZIP engine error,
 	 * APPS need to assert (This is a non recoverable error).
@@ -1916,6 +1917,32 @@ int ipa_q6_pre_shutdown_cleanup(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void ipa_q6_pre_shutdown_cleanup_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	ipa_q6_pre_shutdown_cleanup_impl();
+	pr_info("IPA Q6 cleanup in worker complete\n");
+}
+
+int ipa_q6_pre_shutdown_cleanup(void)
+{
+	struct work_struct work;
+
+	/*
+	 * Closing the last subsystem fd can run this notifier in a task killed
+	 * by init during shutdown. CMA migration aborts on a pending fatal
+	 * signal, even for the four-byte DMA buffer used to clear Q6 tables.
+	 * Always run the mandatory cleanup in a signal-free worker, including
+	 * when a fatal signal arrives after notifier entry.
+	 * Waiting is uninterruptible: the subsystem must not power down until
+	 * all IPA commands and their DMA buffers have completed.
+	 */
+	INIT_WORK_ONSTACK(&work, ipa_q6_pre_shutdown_cleanup_work);
+	queue_work(system_unbound_wq, &work);
+	flush_work(&work);
+	destroy_work_on_stack(&work);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 /**
 * ipa_q6_post_shutdown_cleanup() - A cleanup for the Q6 pipes
 *                    in IPA HW after modem shutdown. This is performed
@@ -4575,4 +4602,3 @@ subsys_initcall(ipa_module_init);
 
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL v2");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("IPA HW device driver");
-
